WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:08.770
So krypton is one of the noble gases, it’s
not very reactive but it does

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:14.330
react with the element fluorine. Jim Turner,
who was my supervisor

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:19.439
when I did my doctorate, was the first person
to discover that fluorine

00:00:19.439 --> 00:00:24.929
could react with krypton but even that reaction
requires quite bright

00:00:24.929 --> 00:00:28.849
lights to break the bond between the fluorine
atoms to get them to

00:00:28.849 --> 00:00:37.550
react. But krypton can also be used in lasers
when mixtures of krypton

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:42.440
and of fluorine-containing compound can be
used to generate very bright

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:48.390
pulses or intense pulses of ultraviolet light.
Some years ago we had a

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:53.420
professor here who bought a really big krypton-fluoride
laser and when

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.070
he switched it on and the beam hit the wall
it burnt a hole right through

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:01.400
the wall so he knew where to make the hole
to get his beam into the

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:01.989
next lab.

